data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":345,"item_id":"fc_0696d7218c76ce25016acbafe86c1087d2a19a9980f7a8edd5","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"Tests launch isolated servers and temporary SQLite databases, checking\",\"newText\":\"Directory tests also verify intersecting filters, read-only rendering, literal notes, invalid-range preservation, ownership and return ordering, navigation defaults, and restart persistence.\\n\\nTests launch isolated servers and temporary SQLite databases, checking\"},{\"oldText\":\"Health check: `GET /health` returns `{\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\"}`.\",\"newText\":\"Health check: `GET /health` returns `{\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\"}`.\\n\\nChoose Task directory on the home page to open `/directory`, a read-only view across projects. Project scope (Active/Archived), Task filter (All/Open/Completed/Deleted), Priority filter, Directory search, and the inclusive due range intersect without changing stored data. Search matches only task titles using the ordinary search rules. Results show the owner, original title, completion, priority, due date, and literal multiline notes in project creation order and stored task order. Open project resets that project's filters; Projects returns home. Each fresh directory opening starts with Active scope, All task/priority filters, and empty search/range.\"}]}"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":346,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0696d7218c76ce25016acbafe86c1087d2a19a9980f7a8edd5","call_id":"call_c5c2a25d353a4654a56fa179d7327140","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"Tests launch isolated servers and temporary SQLite databases, checking\",\"newText\":\"Directory tests also verify intersecting filters, read-only rendering, literal notes, invalid-range preservation, ownership and return ordering, navigation defaults, and restart persistence.\\n\\nTests launch isolated servers and temporary SQLite databases, checking\"},{\"oldText\":\"Health check: `GET /health` returns `{\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\"}`.\",\"newText\":\"Health check: `GET /health` returns `{\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\"}`.\\n\\nChoose Task directory on the home page to open `/directory`, a read-only view across projects. Project scope (Active/Archived), Task filter (All/Open/Completed/Deleted), Priority filter, Directory search, and the inclusive due range intersect without changing stored data. Search matches only task titles using the ordinary search rules. Results show the owner, original title, completion, priority, due date, and literal multiline notes in project creation order and stored task order. Open project resets that project's filters; Projects returns home. Each fresh directory opening starts with Active scope, All task/priority filters, and empty search/range.\"}]}","status":"completed"}}

event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":347,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_0696d7218c76ce25016acbafe1568087d285b20dd0b54eeb83","object":"response","created_at":1791733729,"completed_at":1791733742,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0696d7218c76ce25016acbafe32b5c87d2a2ab0fbeecdea504","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Evaluating code clarity**\n\nI need to focus on avoiding duplication in the range rules for a new function, ensuring clarity. There's no need for excessive complexity. I'll address concerns about notes being visible and handle CSS properties like overflow-wrap and min-width. \n\nThe current code checks for duplicates, which is fine. For legacy tests, it seems like we can add a small assertion, but there’s no need since the upgrade test for the initial database is already covered. After I edit the documentation, I’ll commit the changes."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqy6_o8KQPV0J7h4vJayxL3mJjvkXbLLMhf1Wm3S4oW0XWqY3mmXUjgUTYIggOfZ-SxcjcChwriyvzgcLfDAxM4uss--l1EuONck_bQvGU8dWMf4Lm58BjZcZkC8TA4gm7HwbPREzyLSQKJdBt2-KMiZ1fryn3ckeq15-GmbiZSJU7FBXXzd8TqMzkO8gHnxma_h5Yhk87zyw5l-VewlK8XXlNBB_IM97nBduUJDFbgyHFFoUkpQo-06ZAbkBWq5bQ7O3NeWhDJ-mkbLDalJA66xGvtHVNjkm5gBvmRXFtk0w8_9iwvfg5hhUTLYjSA-rGLgvXUMaXVBx1q1o38UVA5_bEqXPUNCo_-Hqb4nUh-akdFX3pc0t7mkCWXJiW412itAQouW9JIYZd0sHjK30WhRReWG5VM94Jb4p7y_XuqXFNHL-xv7O2VQI-XvaEP_4Fmoq5t8pyP8CtZSS6_I6zjThImBRoLQzdfS0uYUGD7By6M6uy-_ByyuaNZ6az3r4Sw77YVok_AXH8K1Coj8Gwy6WyRhNKsFQOuV9YtPYfNDMj7fgsUwnzmJHQq8MfR6_JQsj03WjTkveXOgt7adxeebQ7Wrk6CiE1RHIFq356ItuIM6cELw-KunqtYB6XlxBsupKBiLM7jQ6vYs78536xNVlusW1TEPU60P_khQdVzNrv3E6LCpzL7NyLIYKRfoXCni31la1C8A8JSzbVRjsshcgMPM4xVuVdGDaKS3FrVRmtq_ze5BNlVJbZS0jNEGXasAHskjZrT0RvecxtaglEr9fe7rvOovyoZIicDvjqvkwI1BTqM3lqEdnCa0Q1_PuzVz0bSrgv98AS2HHj85jVDiOglrzXcxlkSBmCfD_Hhcd4tL_awYkyjzgJUGP4VjH8DDQePYtIbURssevfPljjMmHBVusvkmAUZzfc8KjB4hL-pHFGh7l2b_ekgX22SPhFU-ZUC9HTQcjvwq-cCQgR0gXORiv3pdqfuEMInfEBijPuMOR3owAApu0Dny047onh0ybHpvp-9jv_sMkTgU4NfStQ31xQstgVPP6tAESrTb_l4z7AuOqOJTrBQWAjXOKvG7eEEbJWsGEkbLvUrUErQkcV-yb1SsrGMVYu686PznjFo8r3viCr__pNtJOUY0sSVkdJFeRjxe-js2mGghzlmmbOuPyaq5-QuyimJrKVCgQtYeQ63hzejvMiC2DIyU1dVilrFt-2J9X4_mWu0RM9pkRlArjydFyUTBG0BB-aic1ICjgHvvP3DhgpAnm63N0GFk9bRZorejyy55yRWDyjX85z6J56FOc8107bgEgS5tWmmGk4hGqEajz1jVFQGpWYRg7zCZJ3dp7gDjPHN5cDgBdr9Mas4dhjqAy162VifKCqVijSld9tu5TrbxB8kYXN3Ry5cItfHy8DRSdiggZwxcTN3cr_FablUVDCZ3WgRYirreZzmmQVTBBfi4seBWLlpQqmOeg7GG47L_qSh11HRw4oYAU2p_H46KukhPvQlO1WTGHFGsAL99piUPvO3OEgM-FucdShTH2rTBIUXSKM5AgrgZ-6vMpU2ZT_MNmFy6IjlGfCsLNGPwHlWGqJ_5hrDIsZVLUw678l6DZjgNAFpT0JpW09B59xkxD2z9cRxvkN4AmlZ3Wa3X6zQFoeequldPDoDDC2TwXy--vTntw0it1s3sB_gtzzWEQDDZ-NevRUDPzmm4Dq0NW2wW2r6sLGDlNVt2_TxYU2gBobHjMaOZ_xE-jS_oRsfeL6bM6Xwu6Wu_B8HwWcrQ_T3vAjR0ctjCasmgUgtY6U1_8e3KHUNdA5ZfdbLr0Ft0n16qlYAAEHfZc0vG6KomdPNh48eYKKr4FqnPBRz7